# Biotron public-site refactor memory

## Workflow and repository boundaries

- Work in `Biotron-Site` on `la/general-improvements`. Inspect the current branch and worktree before editing.
- Never push `Biotron-Site` to `origin`. Make small local commits whose subjects tell the review story. Preserve unrelated work.
- `BioTronStyle` may be pushed only when a shared-library change must be published. It is currently consumed at commit `495fe6c`.
- Keep the production-shaped preview container `biotron-site-web-1` running with `restart: unless-stopped` at `http://localhost:5177`, bound to `127.0.0.1`. Rebuild it after each finished change.
- The site is frontend-only. Verify with `npm run build`, the live container, and real browser inspection. Check the exact scroll stop affected by a Three.js change.

## Information architecture and brand

- The top navigation is Projects, Sponsors, Calendar, and Apply. About was removed; Join and Apply were consolidated.
- `/projects` shows current projects first and past projects below. `/past-projects` redirects to `/projects#past`.
- `/sponsors` is a real page. `/calendar` is an intentional placeholder for the future `BiotronCalendar` public feed; do not alter that repo for site-only work.
- Use the shared BioTron wordmark and hand favicon from `@biotron/style`.
- Use black and graphite surfaces. Purple `#160b6c` is the primary highlight; EXO blue `#3050b0` is secondary. Avoid pale blue `#aedbfc` in the site UI.
- Tour-side panels all use the EXO blue rail and white highlight text, including About statistics. Do not restore project-specific panel colors.

## Homepage and workshop

- The hero reads exactly two lines: `Welcome to` then `Biotron.`. Keep the title clear of the first board.
- The hero’s resting offset belongs on `.flythrough__hero-content`; GSAP animates `.flythrough__hero`. Combining both transforms causes a first-pixel scroll jump.
- The About whiteboard is at `[-3.2, 1.9, -3.2]`, faces forward, and the first camera stop targets `[-3.2, 1.8, -3.2]`.
- The workshop has no procedural scatter. Do not restore the random cubes, cylinders, or toruses. Project-model primitives and structural geometry remain.
- Use the native browser cursor. There is no custom cursor layer.
- The four recruitment groups are Mechanical, Electrical, Software, and Outreach & Operations. Software includes firmware, controls, signal processing, machine learning, and tooling.

## Mobile experience

- The approved desktop layout is the reference. Keep mobile fixes scoped to phone and touch breakpoints unless a change is explicitly requested for desktop.
- Phones below 640px use the stacked homepage. Short coarse-pointer viewports also use it so a phone held in landscape never enters the workshop flythrough. Tablets may keep the immersive room.
- Mobile containers keep a 20px minimum gutter and respect safe-area insets. Project-detail specifications use a 2-by-2 grid on phones.
- The mobile menu locks page scrolling while open, closes on Escape and on every menu choice, and marks the current route. Standalone phone controls and footer links keep 44px touch targets.
- The narrow footer places Projects and Team beside one another while Brand and Contact span both columns.

## Voice and contact

- Apply an Elements of Style voice: active, concrete, concise, and undistracted. Omit needless words and do not use em dashes in site copy.
- Facebook is retired and must not appear. Contact uses `biotron@uwaterloo.ca` and Instagram `https://www.instagram.com/uwaterloo_biotron/` (`@uwaterloo_biotron`).
